value, made afresh","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for each iteration.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The unit’s work runs in the signal’s task each time iteration begins; a unit that fails"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the batched sequence with its error. When the batched sequence ends first, the unit’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work is cancelled; a unit whose work ignores cancellation keeps the batch’s internal task"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alive until it returns, though the batched sequence itself ends at once. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" takes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-88w9i","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves the subject alone. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy runs the unit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anew and fires once when it completes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let reachable = DeferredTask { try await server.waitUntilReachable() }","for try await requests in outbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(20), .signal(reachable))) {","    try await send(requests)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes once, when the given unit of work completes."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-5of